{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "075T", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-descent-remark-list-local-source-target}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-base-change-smooth}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-descent-lemma-descending-property-smooth}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-local-source-target}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ba9059a394654589e82780439601c449305f7770a1974afff14a7dc31e7a2ce3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe property ``being smooth'' of morphisms of algebraic\nspaces is smooth local on the source-and-target, see\nDescent on Spaces, Remark <REF_0001>.\nIt is also stable under base change and fpqc local on the target, see\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0002>\nand\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0003>.\nHence, by\nLemma <REF_0004>\nabove, we may define what it means for a morphism of algebraic spaces\nto be smooth as follows and it agrees with the already\nexisting notion defined in\nProperties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0005>\nwhen the morphism is representable by algebraic spaces.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2cfdd8f26e536051af26b4767407b7a4afc0995a730a50ba82cbf35a8ac6f808", "unit_id": "tag:075T:prose-0001"}
